          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Randall-Sumdrum model
            (
            %a{:href => "#RandallSundrum99a"}> Randall-Sundrum 99a
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RandallSundrum99b"} 99b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+inspired+model"} string theory inspired
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28physics%29"} models
            in combined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+physics"} particle physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            constitutes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            of an ambient
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            would pertain to the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de sitter
            “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"}> bulk
            ”
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion+field"} fermion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter+fields"} matter fields
            would be constrained to reside on that boundary, as would hence be all observations made via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+radiation"} electromagnetic radiation
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observers"} observers
            inside this cosmology.
          %p
            Hence the extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
            in these models need not be small (technically: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            spaces need not be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
            with tiny
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observers"} observers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} Kaluza-Klein compactification
            models for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            with extra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
            = succeed "." do
              %em large extra dimension models
          %p
            One original motivation for the RS-models was the idea that this setup could address the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+problem"} hierarchy problem
          %p
            Something at least close to Randall-Sundrum models naturally appears in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            is part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersected
            to a 3+1-dimensional subspace. By the general lore of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbatively
            these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            is qualitatively of Randall-Sundrum form, even if details may differ. For the quick idea see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Teraguchi07"} Teraguchi 07, around slide 21
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Uranga02"} Uranga 02, section 18
          %p
            For more on this see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "intersecting+D-brane+model#Cosmology"} Cosmology and Holography
